# .andromeda/ is the Andromeda pipeline's durable route / state / specs / runs — TRACKED, not ignored.
# (setup-project's first commit captures it; every wrap commits its updates; new-session reads committed state.)
# Conductor's own ephemeral PRODUCT run-artifacts (scenario journals/reports/runs.db) live at /runs/ —
# that is the separate, later ignore target (synthetic-PII-corpus journals), handled at setup/impl, NOT here.

# --- Code-graph cache (the ONE .andromeda/ exception — derived from code, rebuilt by code-graph.py) ---
/.andromeda/cache/
__pycache__/

# --- Rust (andromeda-setup-project) ---
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.iml
# Cargo.lock IS committed — Conductor is a binary workspace (reproducible builds + deterministic cargo-audit).

# --- Conductor run artifacts (synthetic per-run journals/reports/runs.db — generated, not tracked) ---
/runs/

# --- Self-observation logs (ephemeral, truncated per invocation — agent-latest.jsonl, the sibling of /runs/) ---
/logs/

# --- Secrets / env (Conductor owns no secrets — guardrail) ---
# Mirrors the secret-file-name class crates/conductor-core/tests/secret_scan_gate.rs detects, so the ignore
# rules and the gate name the same classes.
.env*
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.key
*.cer
*.crt
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_dsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*

# --- Claude Code ---
.claude/backup/
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- SUT fallout: Pulse emits Specta/TauRPC bindings relative to ITS cwd, so any live probe launching
# pulse-app from this root writes /ui/src/bindings/ here. Foreign artifacts, never Conductor's.
# Recurrence-proof for every future arm.
/ui/

# --- cargo-mutants scratch output. Written to the repo root by any bare `cargo mutants` invocation
# (the audit skill redirects to its run dir with --output; an ad-hoc scoped re-run does not), and it is
# ~40 files of tool state, never Conductor's artifact — an unignored run rides the next `git add -A`.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/
